      "init": {
        "label": "Two-frame plan",
        "body": "# Dependencies as their own table\nA plain **Frame Input** can't hold a list in a cell, so this plan keeps the tasks and their dependencies in two frames. **Tasks** is just Task and Duration. **Links** is one row per dependency: Successor, Predecessor, Type and Lag.\n\nWire both into **Schedule**: the links add to each task's predecessors, and the rest works the same as a Cube plan. A link naming a task that isn't in Tasks is an error.\n\nThe other form is a Cube Input with a Predecessors list cell (see the Remodel example). Use whichever fits your data.",
        "color": "sky",
        "width": 360,
        "height": 250
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tasks",
      "type": "FrameInputNode",
      "x": 60,
